# M13 — Two-Sovereign Internet-Of-Intelligence Proof

Demonstrate useful, voluntary, positive-surplus cooperation between sovereign
institutions while preserving credible exit.

## Why this is next

The single `depends_on` edge is `M12`, which defines the AIIP federation contract — envelopes, terms
discovery and semantic negotiation, federated admission, IFC/disclosure/receipt/settlement binding, dispute
kernel, and portable exit — as contract shape rather than as demonstrated cooperation between separately
administered institutions. M13 exercises that contract across a real sovereignty boundary and prices the
result per participant. `sequence.v1.json` also declares the external gate `independently operated Systems`,
so contract completeness alone does not open this stage.

