## In scope

- `M13.1` run one customer/data-owner System and one independently governed coordinator/worker System, then
  add an independent provider or verifier.
- `M13.2` freeze each participant's outside option, private valuation method, costs, risks, rights, and
  contracted benefit before the trial.
- `M13.3` repeat useful work across the sovereignty boundary without collapsing identities, truth,
  admission, or authority.
- `M13.4` preserve verification, acceptance, attribution, dispute, and exit.
- `M13.5` disclose subsidy and compare against eligible same-domain/direct-local baselines.
- `M13.6` run a negative-surplus control in which a System safely declines and continues locally.
- Preregister System independence, identities, control dependencies, terms root, comparator, and stop rule,
  naming the independent provider or verifier before observation.
- Two-admin product/evidence-export journey over nine ordered transitions — `discover_worker`, `negotiate`,
  `admit_lease`, `perform_work`, `contribute`, `verify_and_accept`, `revoke_or_retire`, `portable_exit`,
  `repeat_and_independence_audit` — each with honest loading, empty, ready, denied/revoked,
  unavailable/degraded, stale/ambiguous, recovery, and completed states, advancing only on canonical owner
  state plus receipt or read-only projection evidence.
- Pulled product: invited cross-organization and Network/Open Goal Space modes, aiagent/sas participation
  surfaces, cross-domain Governance and Provenance.
- Thresholds frozen before observation: full outside-option, cost, risk, and contracted-benefit coverage for
  every required party; positive surplus for every required party and sponsor value above the frozen outside
  option; at least two accepted cross-sovereign cycles; zero independence violations; full subsidy and
  eligible-baseline coverage; at least one safe-decline control; zero unauthorized final-invoker calls and
  zero status-inferred effects.

## Out of scope

- Every M14 obligation: connected/secured services, external demand evidence, network effects, native
  asset, and demand-gated optional L1.
- Definition of the AIIP contract, federated admission modes, and the dispute-adjudication-remedy kernel,
  which M12 owns and M13 only exercises.
- Live embodied promotion, which remains a conditional `FUTURE` record.
- Any configuration where a shared runtime, database, administrator, authority, or continued hosted trust
  supplies the cooperation.
- Cohort-scale or one-shot generalization from a single trial.

